hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17982","Ismail narrated to us, he said, Yunus narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah claimed, he said, Ashajj ibn Asr said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, You have two traits Allah Almighty loves. I said, What are they. He said, Forbearance and modesty. I said, Were they longstanding in me or new. He said, Rather longstanding. I said, Praise be to Allah who fashioned me with two traits He loves."
"17983","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, Awf narrated to us, Abu al-Qamus Zayd ibn Ali narrated to me, he said, One of the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Abd al-Qays narrated to me, he said, And we gifted him among gifts a skin or bag of Tadud or Barni dates. So he said, What is this. We said, This is a gift. He said, And I think he looked at a date of it and returned it to its place, and said, Convey it to the household of Muhammad. He said, The people asked him about things until they asked him about drinks. So he said, Do not drink in a gourd, nor a hantam, nor a naqir, nor a pitched vessel. Drink in a lawful skin tied over its mouth. One of us said to him, O Messenger of Allah, how do you know what a gourd, hantam, naqir, and pitched vessel are. He said, Do I not know what they are. Which Hajar is mightiest. We said, al-Mushaqqar. He said, By Allah, I entered it and took its key. He said, I had forgotten part of his hadith, then Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jarwah reminded me of it. He said, I stood at the spring of al-Zarah. Then he said, O Allah, forgive Abd al-Qays when they submit willingly, not unwilling, not disgraced nor wronged, when some of our people do not submit until disgraced and wronged. He said, And he supplicated facing here from the qiblah, meaning to the right of the qiblah, until he faced the qiblah, then he supplicated for Abd al-Qays, then he said, The best of the people of the east are Abd al-Qays."
"17984","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said, Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Qamus, he said, One of the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, and if he did not say Qays ibn al-Numan, then I have forgotten his name, and he mentioned the hadith. He said, And he supplicated until he faced the qiblah, then he supplicated for Abd al-Qays, then he said, The best of the people of the east in women are Abd al-Qays."
"17985","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Asari narrated to us, he said, Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us that he heard one of the delegation of Abd al-Qays saying, We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they rejoiced greatly at us. When we reached the people they made room for us and we sat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) welcomed us and supplicated for us, then looked at us and said, Who is your chief and leader. So we all pointed to al-Mundhir ibn Aidh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Is this al-Ashajj. And that was the first day this name was given to him, because of a blow on his face by a donkey hoof. So we said, Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Then he stayed behind the people, tied their camels, gathered their goods, then took out his chest, cast off his travel clothes, and wore some of his good clothes. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had stretched his leg and reclined. When al-Ashajj drew near him, the people made room for him and said, Here, O Ashajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upright and drew in his leg and said, Here, O Ashajj. So he sat to the right of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat upright. He welcomed him and treated him kindly, then asked about his land, naming for him Qaryat al-Safa and al-Mushaqqar and other villages of Hajar. So he said, May my father and mother ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, you know the names of our villages better than we do. So he said, I have trodden your lands, and they were opened for me. He said, Then he turned to the Ansar and said, O company of Ansar, honor your brothers, for they are like you in Islam, and most like you in outward and inward. They submitted willingly, not forced nor wronged, when some people refused to submit until they were killed. When he said, How did you see your brothers honoring you and hosting you. They said, The best of brothers; they softened our bedding, made our food good, and night and morning taught us the Book of our Lord and the practice of our Prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased and rejoiced at it. Then he came to us man by man, testing us on what we had learned and knew. Some of us had learned the salutations, and the Opening of the Book, and a surah and two surahs, and a practice and two. Then he turned to us with his face and said, Have you any of your provisions with you. The people rejoiced at that and hastened to their baggage. Each man came with a heap of dates and placed it on a leather mat before him. He gestured with a palm stalk in his hand, over a cubit and under two cubits, which he used as a staff, and said, Do you call this al-Tadud. We said, Yes. Then he gestured to another heap and said, Do you call this al-Sarfan. We said, Yes. Then he gestured to a heap and said, Do you call this al-Barni. So we said, Yes. He said, It is the best of your dates and most beneficial for you. He said, We returned from that delegation and increased planting of it, and our desire for it grew until al-Barni became most of our palms and dates. He said, Al-Ashajj said, O Messenger of Allah, our land is heavy and unhealthy, and if we do not drink these drinks our colors change and our bellies swell. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Do not drink in a gourd, hantam, or naqir. Let one of you drink in his waterskin tied over its mouth. Al-Ashajj said to him, May my father and mother ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, permit us in these. He gestured with his palms and said, O Ashajj, if I permit you in like this, and he said with his palms thus, you would drink it in like this, and he spread and extended his hands, meaning greater than it, until when one of you becomes intoxicated from his drink he rises to his cousin and strikes his leg with a sword. In the delegation was a man from Banu Asr called al-Harith whose leg had been struck in a drinking gathering of theirs in a house; he recited poetry about a woman of them, then one of that household rose and struck his leg with a sword. He said, Al-Harith said, When I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I drew my garment to cover the blow on my leg, though Allah had shown it to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"17986","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Umari narrated to us, he said, Abu Sahl Awf ibn Abi Jamilah narrated to us, from Zayd Abu al-Qamus, from the delegation of Abd al-Qays, that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, O Allah, make us among Your chosen servants, the bright-faced and bright-limbed, the accepted delegation. He said, So they said, O Messenger of Allah, what are the chosen servants of Allah. He said, The righteous servants of Allah. They said, What are the bright-faced and bright-limbed. He said, Those whose ablution spots whiten. They said, What is the accepted delegation. He said, A delegation coming from this nation with their Prophet to their Lord Almighty."
